+    """Plain-tensor form of `_hash_ids_kernel`, for platforms with no Triton.
+
+    Writes `output` in place, shaped [tokens, layers, hash columns]. Every step
+    is a gather, a comparison or a reduction, so a tracing backend lowers it
+    without a custom kernel.
+
+    Two details make the arithmetic safe to write with ordinary operators.
+    `compute_hash_multipliers` bounds each multiplier so `token_id * multiplier`
+    stays inside int64 and stays positive, so the rolling hash never goes
+    negative and `%` agrees with the kernel's C-style remainder. And the
+    per-position history is the same for every layer, so only the rolling hash
+    carries a layer axis.
+    """
+    num_tokens = input_ids.shape[0]
+    num_layers, max_ngram = multipliers.shape
+    num_heads = primes.shape[-1]
+    lookback_depth = lookback_token_ids.shape[1]
+    num_query_rows = query_start_loc.numel() - 1
